    "plain_language": "The paired delta changes sign across the full panel, but the instability is an early-stopping artifact rather than a property of the relational features. On the 2 seeds where both configurations ran to the estimator cap, the delta is +0.00626 with a standard deviation of 0.00051. On the seeds where one configuration stopped early, the delta swings to whichever model kept training, because early stopping selects the round that maximises the very metric being reported. ROC-AUC, which is not the stopping criterion, favours B1-card1 in every seed by +0.00264 with a standard deviation of 0.00052. The relational gain is real; the PR-AUC point estimate is contaminated by the stopping rule and cannot be quoted until the cap is resolved. Seed variance on the delta (0.00615) exceeds the paired-bootstrap standard deviation (0.00199), so the published bootstrap interval understates the true uncertainty: it resamples rows but never refits the model."
